==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de|ru}} {{term|Butterbrot||butterbread, slice of bread with butter|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bʊtɨrˈbrot/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-бутерброд.ogg|audio|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|бутербро́д|m-in|tr=butɛrbród}}

# [[sandwich]], especially an [[open sandwich]]
#* '''1983''', Самуил Маршак (Samuil Marshak), «Баллада о королевском бутерброде» (“Ballad of the King's Bread”), translation of “The King’﻿s Breakfast” by A. A. Milne:
#*: {{ux|ru|— Никто не скажет, бу́дто я / Тиран и сумасброд, / За то, что к чаю я люблю́ / Хороший '''бутерброд'''.|“No one would say that I / Am a tyrant and madman, / For the fact that with my tea I like / A good '''bread-and-butter sandwich'''.”}}

